而这和我在蛇年立下的新年决心是一样的。

459
00:24:31,119 --> 00:24:34,119
It's the same with the year of the cow, the rabbit.
在牛年、兔年也是一样的。

460
00:24:34,119 --> 00:24:39,119
People started to, I think we started to put less and less pressure on ourselves, you know,
人们开始，我想我们开始对自己施加的压力越来越少，

461
00:24:39,119 --> 00:24:42,119
because every day we have a resolution.
因为我们每天都有一个决心。

462
00:24:42,119 --> 00:24:48,119
I've stopped. I have completely given up on making a list of things that I wanted to accomplish for the new year.
我已经停止了。我彻底放弃了列出新年想要完成的事项清单。

463
00:24:48,119 --> 00:24:56,119
And I think images or mistakes like the crying horse become popular because it's for a good laugh.
我认为像哭泣的马这样的图片或错误之所以流行，是因为它们能带来欢乐。

464
00:24:56,119 --> 00:25:02,119
And people are coming to terms with the fact that we don't always have to strive to be the best
人们正在接受这样一个事实：我们并不总是必须争取成为最优秀的，

465
00:25:02,119 --> 00:25:04,119
if everybody's the best, nobody's the best.
如果每个人都是最优秀的，那就没有人是最优秀的。

466
00:25:04,119 --> 00:25:09,119
And when things like this, I thought the crying horse got popular because,
而当出现这种情况时，我觉得哭泣的马之所以走红，是因为，

467
00:25:09,119 --> 00:25:16,119
I don't know if it was just me, but you know when like little kids go like, hmm, and you just go, oh, you're so cute.
我不知道是不是只有我这么觉得，但你知道，当小孩子们发出‘嗯’的声音时，你会忍不住说，哦，你真可爱。

468
00:25:16,119 --> 00:25:23,119
I think that's why this horse went like really popular, because there's supposed to be like a happy kitty looking image.
我想这就是这匹马会如此走红的原因，因为它本应呈现出一种快乐小猫的形象。

469
00:25:23,119 --> 00:25:26,119
What's special about it, right? What's special about a normal...
它有什么特别之处，对吧？普通的……有什么特别的？

470
00:25:26,119 --> 00:25:28,119
Exactly, exactly.
正是如此，正是如此。

471
00:25:28,119 --> 00:25:31,119
You know when people say like, when there's a crack, that's where the light comes in.
你知道人们常说，裂缝就是光线进入的地方。

472
00:25:31,119 --> 00:25:35,119
This is the crack of toy making, the light came into the horse.
这就是玩具制造的裂缝，光线照进了这匹马。

473
00:25:35,119 --> 00:25:37,119
Yeah, I can agree more.
是的，我非常赞同。

474
00:25:37,119 --> 00:25:44,119
I think the mistake makes the horse from a regular merchandise to an intellectual property, right?
我认为这个错误让这匹马从普通商品变成了知识产权，对吗？

475
00:25:44,119 --> 00:25:46,119
Because it makes it unique.
因为它使其独一无二。

476
00:25:46,119 --> 00:25:48,119
That's deep.
真是深刻。

477
00:25:48,119 --> 00:25:53,119
Because as the host was saying, you can buy a smiley horse everywhere,
正如主持人所说，你可以在任何地方买到笑脸马，

478
00:25:53,119 --> 00:25:59,119
but for these upside down, like sad horse giving you the side eyes, it's unique.
但这些倒立的、带着悲伤眼神的马却很独特。

479
00:25:59,119 --> 00:26:04,119
When you put it on the desk, it unravels a bunch of conversations and stories.
当你把它放在桌上，它会引发一连串的对话和故事。

480
00:26:04,119 --> 00:26:12,119
It can spur interest, it's a shareable object with a lot of experience,
它能激发兴趣，是一个充满体验的可分享物品，

481
00:26:12,119 --> 00:26:14,119
a lot of stories behind it.
背后有许多故事。

482
00:26:14,119 --> 00:26:17,119
So I think that's also what makes this crying horse special.
所以我认为这也是让这匹哭泣的马与众不同的原因。

483
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:19,119
I already placed my order.
我已经下单了。

484
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:21,119
I'm buying two actually.
其实我买了两个。

485
00:26:21,119 --> 00:26:27,119
Yeah, I think there's something very deep about it, but you have put it in an excellent term.
是的，我觉得这背后有很深的意义，但你用一个很好的词来表达。

486
00:26:27,119 --> 00:26:29,119
It's the cracks in life where we're lying.
正是生活的裂缝让我们躺在其中。

487
00:26:29,119 --> 00:26:35,119
But again, right now everything happening so fast, a lot of new inventions,
但再次强调，现在一切发展得很快，出现了许多新发明，

488
00:26:35,119 --> 00:26:41,119
a lot of new things happening, and of course the stress is very much on.
各种新事物层出不穷，当然压力也非常大。

489
00:26:41,119 --> 00:26:48,119
Anyway, behind all of the creativeness, all of the cracks in life,
总之，在所有创造力和生活的裂缝背后，

490
00:26:48,119 --> 00:26:52,119
what does it tell us about the state of the Chinese society at this moment?
这向我们揭示了当下中国社会的何种状态？

491
00:26:52,119 --> 00:26:54,119
I know it gets a little heavy.
我知道这有点沉重。

492
00:26:54,119 --> 00:27:03,119
Yeah, but it's a very, very interesting and meaningful question to be posed at this stage in history.
是的，但这是在历史此阶段提出的一个非常非常有趣且有意义的问题。

493
00:27:03,119 --> 00:27:11,119
I think China is in a process of deep change, in my opinion,
我认为，中国正处于深刻变革的进程中，

494
00:27:11,119 --> 00:27:20,119
from just being, so to speak, the factory of the world and to produce goods to be sold outside of China,
从仅仅可以说是世界工厂、生产供国外销售的商品，

495
00:27:20,119 --> 00:27:31,119
but also to develop the creativity or these opportunities that lie in the individual creativity of people further,
而且还在进一步开发个人创造力中蕴含的创意与机遇。

496
00:27:31,119 --> 00:27:34,119
because then consumption will be raised.
因为那时消费会提升。

497
00:27:34,119 --> 00:27:37,119
So if people start to have more hobbies, for example,
所以如果人们开始拥有更多爱好，例如，

498
00:27:37,119 --> 00:27:45,119
and also start to search for meaning in artistic ways besides their normal everyday jobs,
并且在日常工作之外，以艺术方式寻找意义，

499
00:27:46,119 --> 00:27:51,119
this is a surplus for a domestic economy, right?
这对国内经济来说是一种盈余，对吧？

500
00:27:51,119 --> 00:27:54,119
You could say it's a cultural economy in that sense.
从这个意义上说，可以说它是文化经济。

501
00:27:54,119 --> 00:28:00,119
And at the same time it helps to preserve traditions and cultural memory,
同时它有助于保护传统和文化记忆，

502
00:28:00,119 --> 00:28:06,119
so it's a win-win-win in many respects compared to other parts of the world.
因此与世界其他地区相比，它在许多方面是三赢的。

503
00:28:06,119 --> 00:28:10,119
China is still booming and has so much potential.
中国仍在蓬勃发展，潜力巨大。

504
00:28:11,119 --> 00:28:19,119
Although we have this horse, I'm optimistic about China.
虽然我们有这匹马，但我对中国持乐观态度。

505
00:28:19,119 --> 00:28:26,119
And I think this is maybe a good symbol also because, of course, optimism also has to be self-critical, right?
我认为这也许是一个很好的象征，因为乐观当然也必须自我批判，对吧？

506
00:28:26,119 --> 00:28:29,119
It's optimistic on the inside. It's just not showing.
它在内心是乐观的，只是没有表现出来。

507
00:28:29,119 --> 00:28:30,619
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是的，是的，是的。

508
00:28:30,119 --> 00:28:36,119
So and you have to reflect on developments, right?
所以你必须反思发展，对吧？

509
00:28:36,119 --> 00:28:41,119
So it's not like always to pretend to be happy, right?
所以并不是总要假装开心，对吧？

510
00:28:41,119 --> 00:28:43,119
No, no, you've got to be genuinely happy.
不，不，你必须真心快乐。

511
00:28:43,119 --> 00:28:45,119
Yeah, yeah, yeah, you cannot pretend to be happy.
是啊，是啊，是啊，你不能假装开心。

512
00:28:45,119 --> 00:28:51,119
Let's wrap up for the time being for this part of the special edition of The Point with me, Lu Xin.
让我们先暂时结束本期《锐评》特别版，我是卢欣。

513
00:28:51,119 --> 00:28:58,119
Thanks so much to David Bartosz, Alex, Shi and Lelun for a very interesting discussion.
非常感谢David Bartosz、Alex、Shi和Lelun的精彩讨论。

514
00:28:58,119 --> 00:29:06,119
That's it for part one of the special series on the New Year of the Horse, coming to you from The Point with me, Lu Xin.
以上就是《锐评》关于马年新春特别系列第一部分的内容，我是卢欣。

515
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:11,119
More engaging discussions are coming up in our next episode, so don't miss it.
更多精彩讨论将在下一期呈现，敬请期待。

516
00:29:11,119 --> 00:29:14,119
As always, you can follow me on Facebook and X using the handle Lu Xin in Beijing.
一如既往，您可以在 Facebook 和 X 上关注我，用户名是卢欣（北京）。

517
